aise for its engrossing world building and political storytelling, and, of course, the cast's rather generous &quot;assets&quot;. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3768170/extras/67928b4c0717b10be1879f95630293c7.poster.avif?t=1765012387\" aria-label=\"Well-endowed with political intrigue!\" width=780 height=496 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3768170/extras/67928b4c0717b10be1879f95630293c7.webm?t=1765012387\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3768170/extras/67928b4c0717b10be1879f95630293c7.mp4?t=1765012387\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Funbag Fantasy 4 - Brother Astor</i></strong>, takes place in the medieval Kingdom of Litova 400 years prior to the events of the original <strong><i>Funbag Fantasy</i></strong>. Litovia finds itself in a difficult political situation with the ever increasing hostilities of the Confederation of Minotaur Tribes on its border, and the neighboring Kingdom of Armekia unwilling to form an alliance against them unless the Litovian queen agrees to wed their king\u2014\u2014an offer with deep implications for the religious faction Litovia belongs to, and a price they deem too high to pay. Out of other options, the queen of Litovia is forced to order the monasteries on the border to organize to reenforce the kingdom's defenses. One such monastery is Berensch, to which brother Astor, our protagonist, belongs... Will the queen's decision save or doom her kingdom? And what will become of brother Astor?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3768170/extras/37925df96e65eaed